+An optional `serverEnd` line supplies `health`, `foodLevel`, `saturationLevel`, `exhaustion` and `foodTickTimer` from one atomic `data get entity` reply. `serverTickOffset` is the number of server game ticks since the final recorded `gameTime`. The reader compares resources only for an explicit zero offset and prints why other snapshots are skipped, including legacy snapshots without an offset. Game-time queries bracket the read; a read spanning ticks has a null offset and `serverTickOffsetMin`/`serverTickOffsetMax` bounds. Float fields support raw bits. Initial server resources, including the timer, go in `player`. The replay prints how many server snapshots it checked. Client game time is synchronized from server packets, so matching clocks alone does not prove packet-level alignment or establish the server-resource part of L0.
 
